                                                Calm World – Worldwide Wellness & Mindfulness Resource
Planning Document (for submission)

1. Project Title
Calm World – Simple, free mindfulness practices for everyone on Earth.
2. Purpose & Rationale (Why I am building this website)

-Over 1 billion people worldwide experience stress or anxiety (WHO data).
-Many cannot afford paid apps, therapy, or classes, especially in low-income countries.
-Mindfulness techniques are proven to reduce stress, yet most resources are locked behind paywalls or language barriers.
-This website removes all barriers: no cost, no login, no ads, works on any device with internet, and uses universally understood, culture-neutral practices.

3. Target Audience
-Global population (anyone with internet access)
Primary focus:

-People in developing and developed countries alike
-Ages 13–70
-Low-bandwidth users (site is lightweight, <1 MB total)
-Non-English speakers in the future (structure ready for translation)

4. Global Reach Strategy

-Content deliberately culture-neutral or explicitly multicultural (practices from six continents)
-Simple language (short sentences, no jargon)
-Mobile-first responsive design (over 60% of global traffic is mobile)
-Fast loading even on 2G/3G connections
-All resources linked are free and available worldwide

5. Scope

-5 separate static HTML pages (pure HTML + CSS, no JavaScript)
-One shared CSS file for consistency
-Full-screen high-quality purple background image (fixed) that creates a calm atmosphere

6. Technology Choices

-HTML5 + CSS3 only → maximum compatibility and speed
-Semantic HTML for accessibility and SEO
-No frameworks → demonstrates understanding of core web technologies
-Hosted later on free platforms (GitHub Pages / Netlify) → truly global availability

7. Accessibility & Inclusivity Features

-High-contrast white text on dark purple background
-Large, readable fonts
-Proper heading hierarchy (h1 → h2 → etc.)
-Alt text ready for future images
-Works with screen readers
-Keyboard-navigable links

8. Content Summary

-Home: Welcome + mission
-Daily Practices: 10 universal techniques anyone can do in 1–5 minutes
-World Traditions: 6 short mindfulness practices from different continents
-Free Resources: 10+ permanent free tools and links
-About: Explanation of the project and global purpose

9. Visual Design Rationale

-Fixed full-screen purple abstract image → instantly creates calm, meditative mood
-Semi-transparent content overlay → excellent readability while keeping the atmosphere
-Minimalist layout → reduces cognitive load and works worldwide regardless of screen size

10. Success Criteria

-Anyone on Earth with internet can open the site and immediately find a free way to feel calmer
-Zero cost to user and zero cost to maintain
-Demonstrates clean HTML/CSS coding, planning, and global thinking

